me":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T15:06:40-07:00","id":1218699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1005346-does-anyone-remember-blood-at-dawn?p=1218634#post1218634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lucky you, your sis is aawesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, she is. The best in the world. She also bought me 1st edition of Storyteller's Screen for Mage: the Ascension (the one with Angel of Mercy adventure), another rarity for cWoD.<br /> <br /> But, as I wrote earlier, I was wondering why White Wolf/Storyteller's Vault/DriveThruRPG didn't put those adventures in PDF for buy/download for free. And I've got an idea: judging by availability of those items on Ebay maybe they don't have physical copies to scan. So I will write to them and ask it they want me to send them scans so they could put them on their sites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-14-2018, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T07:53:50-07:00","id":1218914,"title":"","content":"I've just recieved an answer from DriveThruRPG about making those adventures available. They said that each publisher manages their products so it's White Wolf decision not to sell them. As my mail was passed to DriveThruRPG's publisher Division and they will discuss it with WW I will wait a few days for an answer what to do from now on. If I won't get any answer I will contact WW about it. I will keep you inform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T09:01:23-07:00","id":1218937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1005346-does-anyone-remember-blood-at-dawn?p=1218914#post1218914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've just recieved an answer from DriveThruRPG about making those adventures available. They said that each publisher manages their products so it's White Wolf decision not to sell them. As my mail was passed to DriveThruRPG's publisher Division and they will discuss it with WW I will wait a few days for an answer what to do from now on. If I won't get any answer I will contact WW about it. I will keep you inform.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks a bunch, most certainly interested in knowing what comes out of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T09:18:43-07:00","id":1218942,"title":"","content":"I love the weirdness of Vampire 1st Edition, especially the setting of Chicago (and by extension, Gary and Milwaukee) from that era. And this is something I did not know about.<br /> <br /> Now I need to find a copy of the 1E Storyteller's Screen with this module.<br /> <br /> Another interesting module from 1E that I used to own is Blood Nativity, set in Cleveland, Ohio. It was one of the few Classic WoD books not published by White Wolf directly, instead being licensed out to Atlas Games. The only other third-party WoD materials from that time frame were the GURPS adaptations of Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage (which were good in their own right as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T10:16:05-07:00","id":1218954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1005346-does-anyone-remember-blood-at-dawn?p=1218942#post1218942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the weirdness of Vampire 1st Edition, especially the setting of Chicago (and by extension, Gary and Milwaukee) from that era. And this is something I did not know about.<br /> <br /> Now I need to find a copy of the 1E Storyteller's Screen with this module.<br /> <br /> Another interesting module from 1E that I used to own is Blood Nativity, set in Cleveland, Ohio. It was one of the few Classic WoD books not published by White Wolf directly, instead being licensed out to Atlas Games. The only other third-party WoD materials from that time frame were the GURPS adaptations of Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage (which were good in their own right as well).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, good luck in that. 2 advices: if you find one read the item description very careful. There are many Storyteller's Screens 1st Edition, but without booklets. And try to find it as frequent as it's possible. I found mine by searching for Blood by dawn every 2 weeks (average auction time on allegro, kind of ebay in Poland) and finally found it on british ebay. Or you can wait for DriveThru answer.<br /> <br /> I like Chicago setting too. Especially with Werewolf (from Under a Blood Red Moon), hunters (from Inquisition supplement) and Mage (from Book of Chantries and possibly Destiny's Price) add ons. But IMHO war between werewolves and Cainites from UaBRM would destroy it tearing the Masquerade apart (I employed Technocracy Damage Control to Clean this mess). But games after the war, when PCs tried to win this domain for themselves was very exciting. As for Blood Nativity it was the standing point for my Chicago campaign. After BN players decided to take their destiny into their own hands and went to Gary searching for a place where they could hehehe live :P.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T11:11:10-07:00","id":1218968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1005346-does-anyone-remember-blood-at-dawn?p=1218954#post1218954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO war between werewolves and Cainites from UaBRM would destroy it tearing the Masquerade apart (I employed Technocracy Damage Control to Clean this mess). But games after the war, when PCs tried to win this domain for themselves was very exciting. As for Blood Nativity it was the standing point for my Chicago campaign. After BN players decided to take their destiny into their own hands and went to Gary searching for a place where they could hehehe live :P.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think the Chicago vampires could cover up things like this on their own through manipulation of mortal institutions like news coverage and police as things like gang violence or just flat out coverups of whole incidents with dominate. I find the Sabbat far more problematic to the Masquerade with roving packs of killers, mass embraces, monstrous war ghouls, etc... in random places where safeguards either wouldn't be in place or were eaten by said Sabbat packs of roaming killers not to mention things getting caught on camera in any city it's pretty unavoidable nowadays.<br /> <br /> Sabbat fiction has been fun to read and watch evolve but for me much of it left the World of Darkness long ago.<br /> <br /> More on topic I remember this adventure as being a stark contrast to the personalities given in the first Gary adventure. Is this the one where the sweet innocent never speaks vampire looking for love does a 180 and is a stripper and the really old Gangrel did a 180 personality wise as well if I remember correctly but I do hope they reprint it so I can reread it for fun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T12:30:19-07:00","id":1219004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1005346-does-anyone-remember-blood-at-dawn?p=1218968#post1218968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually think the Chicago vampires could cover up things like this on their own through manipulation of mortal institutions like news coverage and police as things like gang violence or just flat out coverups of whole incidents with dominate. I find the Sabbat far more problematic to the Masquerade with roving packs of killers, mass embraces, monstrous war ghouls, etc... in random places where safeguards either wouldn't be in place or were eaten by said Sabbat packs of roaming killers not to mention things getting caught on camera in any city it's pretty unavoidable nowadays.<br /> <br /> Sabbat fiction has been fun to read and watch evolve but for me much of it left the World of Darkness long ago.<br /> <br /> More on topic I remember this adventure as being a stark contrast to the personalities given in the first Gary adventure. Is this the one where the sweet innocent never speaks vampire looking for love does a 180 and is a stripper and the really old Gangrel did a 180 personality wise as well if I remember correctly but I do hope they reprint it so I can reread it for fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, Camarilla could cover the violence but I don't think that they could explain war ghouls, red rain or sick swans flying in the sky. Media blackout doesn't resolve this problem and a few other groups than Technocracy have sientists respected enough to explain those phenomenons. Plus Technocracy have MiBs, so if anyone start to run screaming about monsters (help, there was Vohzd on my backyard) BLINK, problem solved.<br /> <br /> As for Blood at dawn I will read it in about a month and I'm dying to do it. As for reprint I hope that you all have the same chance as I have to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-16-2018, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T06:01:42-07:00","id":1219600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1005346-does-anyone-remember-blood-at-dawn?p=1218942#post1218942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The only other third-party WoD materials from that time frame were the GURPS adaptations of Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage (which were good in their own right as well).</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot about France by Night (I don't remember the publisher, but as far as I know it is considered canon) and a few German suplements. And of course Moonstone comic books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-17-2018, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T07:37:16-07:00","id":1219631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1005346-does-anyone-remember-blood-at-dawn?p=1219600#post1219600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You forgot about France by Night (I don't remember the publisher, but as far as I know it is considered canon) and a few German suplements. And of course Moonstone comic books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't know about the France by Night book. I did know about the Moonstone comics, but I was just talking in terms of direct RPG materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T08:58:26-07:00","id":1219668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1005346-does-anyone-remember-blood-at-dawn?p=1219631#post1219631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I didn't know about the France by Night book. I did know about the Moonstone comics, but I was just talking in terms of direct RPG materials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there were a few sourcebook created by people from countries other than USA later &quot;adopted&quot; by WW (like FbN describing all aspects of WoD: garous, Cainites etc.). We tried the same in Poland but players from different cities couldn't agree in so many things that project died long ago. All that remained is a few pages about werewolf caerns, 2 cities for V:tM and one main chantry. Of course it isn't canon but I still merge this with official metaplot (I think it wasn't nad after all). As for Moonstone comic books I haven't read any but I've they're quite good.<br /> <br /> As for RPG materials what do you think about Vampire Redemption, Bloodlines, Hunter: the Reckoning series and canceled Werewolf: the Apocalypse video games? And Kindred: the Embraced short series?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T09:21:37-07:00","id":1219674,"title":"","content":"I love Bloodlines and the Hunter: The Reckoning PS2 game as well (in fact, the latter was my introduction to White Wolf's IP) and I would love to play Redemption one day.<br /> <br /> As for Kindred: The Embraced, it was good for what it was (a 90's Soap Opera take on WoD) and served as a nice introduction to Vampire for me when SyFy aired reruns of it for Halloween back in the late 2000's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T09:45:41-07:00","id":1219683,"title":"","content":"IMHO Bloodlines is a decent game. I use Ashcroft as a hometown of one of my player's character (love the town's history). I have to admit that I'm considering buying PS2 only for this game (to copy map of Ashcroft also and check if there is some info in which state it lies). As for Reckoning I think it's a wasted chance. The idea of chasing true love for 800 years is great, but after spending this time under the debris would drive the main character crazy. Also I don't like hack&amp;slash games and gameplay of Redemption is like Diablo's: clean the level, back to town, sell items and go to another level. Not to mention historical/continuity error.<br /> <br /> As for Kindred I think it was quite good, especially Fiori-Luna conflict and the ending. And by lucky coincidence I got a copy of &quot;A fatal case&quot; book, written after Mark Frankel's death by somebody of the crew describing Julian's history and wereabouts after the end of the show. It wasn't published thought, only printed in maybe 50 copies to distribute among the rest of the crew.<br /> <br /> I don't know how well you know Werewolf setting but if you do watch this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rSN6Cbct2GQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rSN6Cbct2GQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rSN6Cbct2GQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/rSN6Cbct2GQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All cutscenes from cancelled Werewolf video game. After some upgrades it became great adventure for one of my players (however didn't end well). Now I'm dying to see this upcoming W:tA game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T13:25:24-07:00","id":1239783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1005346-does-anyone-remember-blood-at-dawn?p=1218937#post1218937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks a bunch, most certainly interested in knowing what comes out of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>All right ladies and gentelmen. Few days ago I recieved reply from WW about booklets. They said that propably don't have those booklet files or they are poor quality. But they are interested so I will scan them and send them to WW so MAYBE they will be available at DTRPG.com. But be patient, my computer's broken so I could scan them when I will visit my parents. Maybe next week I will send them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T16:36:06-07:00","id":1239834,"title":"","content":"Maybe some of you or your friends have a copy of another booklet, this time from ST Screen for 2nd edition Vampire the Masquerade, called Contacts and Victims? If yes maybe he/she could also send a scan to WW so they could put it on DTRPG.com?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T16:53:01-07:00","id":1239841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbc