 (to copy map of Ashcroft also and check if there is some info in which state it lies). As for Reckoning I think it's a wasted chance. The idea of chasing true love for 800 years is great, but after spending this time under the debris would drive the main character crazy. Also I don't like hack&amp;slash games and gameplay of Redemption is like Diablo's: clean the level, back to town, sell items and go to another level. Not to mention historical/continuity error.<br /> <br /> As for Kindred I think it was quite good, especially Fiori-Luna conflict and the ending. And by lucky coincidence I got a copy of &quot;A fatal case&quot; book, written after Mark Frankel's death by somebody of the crew describing Julian's history and wereabouts after the end of the show. It wasn't published thought, only printed in maybe 50 copies to distribute among the rest of the crew.<br /> <br /> I don't know how well you know Werewolf setting but if you do watch this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rSN6Cbct2GQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rSN6Cbct2GQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rSN6Cbct2GQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/rSN6Cbct2GQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All cutscenes from cancelled Werewolf video game. After some upgrades it became great adventure for one of my players (however didn't end well). Now I'm dying to see this upcoming W:tA game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would love a <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bloodlines 2 and I hope the upcoming W:tA game is like Bloodlines in play style (a open world RPG)</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12439-the-vampire-fish","name":"The Vampire Fish","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T21:23:38-07:00","id":1240320,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines is a very fun game and i have toyed with a number of its NPCs and ideas, with some retouches and twists, in Masquerade and Requiem games both.<br /> I agree that <i>Redemption </i>has its ups and downs but sometimes that's good too, you get a wonky storyline or two, cut the fat and/or rotten bits makes something bigger and your own with the new set of pieces at hand.<br /> <br /> A friend has made a very interesting by combining Redepmtion with Transylvania Chronicles - and setting all scenes in New York (and NY by Night, that's chockfull of Transylvania by Night survivors to a crazy degree) in Saint Petesburg instead.<br /> We have also been doing a weird kindred-centric rewrite of sorts of Rage Across Russia along the way with quite entertaining results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-30-2018, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:43:50-07:00","id":1240481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> 