s: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 07-30-2018, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T13:36:22-07:00","id":1240569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1005346-does-anyone-remember-blood-at-dawn?p=1240481#post1240481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fun fact, the italian version of &quot;the Final nights&quot; (a sorta compendium of Thin Blood, Nights of Prophecy and a couple other supplements) has a whole &quot;local&quot; chapter describing the Italian's Cainite landscape. I never found where it was taken from, so my theory is that they wrote it down based on the tales of the &quot;official&quot; vampire LARP web</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seeing that and France By Night translated to english and in PDF on Drivethru or some other place would be nice indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T15:31:48-07:00","id":1240610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1005346-does-anyone-remember-blood-at-dawn?p=1240320#post1240320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines is a very fun game and i have toyed with a number of its NPCs and ideas, with some retouches and twists, in Masquerade and Requiem games both.<br /> I agree that <i>Redemption </i>has its ups and downs but sometimes that's good too, you get a wonky storyline or two, cut the fat and/or rotten bits makes something bigger and your own with the new set of pieces at hand.<br /> <br /> A friend has made a very interesting by combining Redepmtion with Transylvania Chronicles - and setting all scenes in New York (and NY by Night, that's chockfull of Transylvania by Night survivors to a crazy degree) in Saint Petesburg instead.<br /> We have also been doing a weird kindred-centric rewrite of sorts of Rage Across Russia along the way with quite entertaining results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I didn't say that W:tM-R was entirely bad. I just think that a big potential has been wasted. When I heard for the first time about this game I thought that it will be something like Transylvania or Giovanni Chronicles, a few levels for each century and cutscenes describing downtime. As for NPCs it has some non/ anti canon elements (for example Azhra is described in Transylvania by Night and is a very old and powerful Cainite resembling Vukodlak). But there were some interesting characters like Luther Black or Otto (London arms dealer). Another flaw: some historical inacuracies (the game is set in 1148, and Swordbrethren were founded almost 60 years later and, as far as I know, cut their hair short, grew beards and never fought in Bohemia). But I still used NPCs during my games. I love mix of video games and tabletop. During my campaign Serena (from V:tM-R) as a PC survived Transylvania and Giovanni Chronicle (yeah, I merged them; PCs from each of them met in Silchester), when Christof awoke in London she rushed to meet him (she was late). There she almost met Ryan McCullough (from cancelled Werewolf: the Apocalypse Heart of Gaia game; he was the one who attacked Christof near the Tower of London; I assumed that after the opening cutscene from Heart of Gaia he attacked the first creature he intinctively sensed as an enemy). Ryan in turn was born in Ashcroft (from Hunter series) just like Heather Poe (from Bloodlines, IMHO it is very possible that they are the same age). That's why he attacked PC from Bloodlines, out of pure jealousy. Heck, I even used Football Manager series so my players could bet (and Diarmid &quot;Mad Dog&quot; Dunsirn from pregenerated characters for V:TM is an ex Celtic Glasgow coach) and Truck Driver game when my characters was a driver (he also participate in underground street racing circle so I could use NFS series ]:-&gt; ).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 07-07-2019, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T15:19:41-07:00","id":1322653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1005346-does-anyone-remember-blood-at-dawn?p=1218634#post1218634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lucky you, your sis is aawesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, my sister is double awesome. Today I recieved my copy of V:TM Storyteller's Screen, 2nd edition, with booklet <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I found it and she bought it (the seller didn't want to send it to Poland but UK was ok). I tell ya, if I ever move to England too I will find a way to change her mind about RPG (I was very succesful in scaring her away; you know, sibling's rivalry) and there will be another Elysium/sept/chantry/freehold (and propably all of them) there, in Burton upon Trent. And maybe some LARPs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 07-06-2019, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T12:08:14-07:00","id":1509510,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13141\" data-vbnamecard=\"13141\">Nail Eater</a><br /> <br /> I take it this is not going to happen? It's like the Victorian Age trilogy not getting on Kindle. Why can't we have nice things??? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}